{"id":"a7","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":13,"of":19,"title":"In, to, from","titleHe":"מִלּוֹת יַחַס","goal":"Attach בְּ, לְ and מִ, and combine them with the article.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Three of the commonest prepositions are single letters glued to the front of the word: בְּ in or at, לְ to, מִ from."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"בְּבַיִת","en":"in a house"},{"he":"לְעִיר","en":"to a city"},{"he":"מִסֵּפֶר","en":"from a book"}]},{"type":"text","body":"When the word is definite, the הַ doesn't survive alongside them — it merges into the preposition's vowel."},{"type":"table","caption":"With the article","head":["indefinite","definite"],"rows":[["בְּבַיִת — in a house","בַּבַּיִת — in the house"],["לְעִיר — to a city","לָעִיר — to the city"],["מִבַּיִת — from a house","מֵהַבַּיִת — from the house"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"מִ is the exception: it keeps the הַ visible and lengthens its own vowel instead — מֵהַבַּיִת, not מַבַּיִת."}],"vocab":[{"he":"בְּ","en":"in, at","translit":"be-"},{"he":"לְ","en":"to, for","translit":"le-"},{"he":"מִ","en":"from","translit":"mi-"},{"he":"עִם","en":"with","translit":"im"},{"he":"אֶל","en":"to, towards","translit":"el"},{"he":"בֵּין","en":"between","translit":"bein"},{"he":"לְיַד","en":"next to","translit":"leyad"},{"he":"תַּחַת","en":"under","translit":"tachat"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["a hero, a mighty man","finds","daughter","in, at"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בְּ","translit":"be-"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["fire","to, for","market","to learn"],"correct":1,"prompt":"לְ","translit":"le-"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["from","fruit","my name","bathroom, bath"],"correct":0,"prompt":"מִ","translit":"mi-"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["yellow","the ceremony closing the Sabbath","with","healthy"],"correct":2,"prompt":"עִם","translit":"im"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["to, towards","summer","childhood","silence, stillness"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אֶל","translit":"el"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["how much, how many","closes","between","nice"],"correct":2,"prompt":"בֵּין","translit":"bein"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["new","next to","restaurant","an appointed festival"],"correct":1,"prompt":"לְיַד","translit":"leyad"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “to, for”?","options":["חֲצָאִית","בְּוַדַּאי","שָׁלוֹם","לְ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “between”?","options":["בֵּין","אַחַר כָּךְ","טָעִים","חֶבְרָה"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"לְיַד","translit":"leyad","en":"next to"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["בֵּין","מִ","אֶל","עִם"],"correct":2,"say":"אֶל","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “from”?","options":["שְׂמֹאלָה","מִ","קָם","כָּשֵׁר"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["בְּ","in, at"],["לְ","to, for"],["מִ","from"],["עִם","with"],["אֶל","to, towards"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"“In the city” is —","options":["בָּעִיר","בְּהָעִיר","בַּעִיר","בְּעִיר"],"correct":0,"why":"The article merges into the preposition; because עִיר starts with ע the vowel is kamatz, giving בָּעִיר. בְּעִיר without it means in a city."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “under”?","options":["תַּחַת","בֵּיצָה","סַבְלָנוּת","מְאֹד"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “in, at” in Hebrew","answer":"בְּ","hint":"be-"}]}